course: dictionary
lesson: 10770
title: Ultraviolet light
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: UV is short for ultraviolet, a kind of light that comes from the Sun. Our eyes cannot see it, so you cannot tell it is there just by looking. «You cannot feel UV rays, so you can burn even when it does not feel hot.» That is why sunburn can happen on a cool day.
explain: UV can burn your skin and hurt your eyes. Over many years it can also damage skin and cause skin cancer, so protecting yourself matters. The UV index is a number that tells you how strong the Sun's UV is on a given day: the higher the number, the stronger the UV.
explain: UV is strongest around midday, in summer, near the equator, high up in mountains, and near water or snow. It can still be strong on cloudy days, so do not judge it by the sky. When the UV index is 3 or higher, use sun protection: sunscreen, a hat, sunglasses and shade.
fact: UV stands for ultraviolet, a kind of light from the Sun.
fact: UV light is invisible: our eyes cannot see it.
fact: UV rays can burn skin and hurt eyes.
fact: The UV index is a number that shows how strong the Sun's UV is.
fact: UV lamps are used to kill germs.
exercise: What does UV stand for? | Under Very | Umbrella Vest | Unusual Violet | *Ultraviolet
exercise: Why can you get sunburnt on a cool day? | Because the sunscreen has worn off the bottle | *Because UV rays cannot be felt, even when it does not feel hot | Because the wind blows the heat onto you | Because you were swimming in the sea
exercise: When is UV usually strongest? | Early in the morning in autumn | Only on very hot, dry days in the desert | *Around midday in summer | At night in winter
test: Which of these can UV light do? | Lift you up off the ground | Make a rainbow in the sky | Make a sound | *Hurt your eyes
test: What does the UV index tell you? | How hot the air is | How many clouds are in the sky | *How strong the Sun's UV is on a given day | How much rain will fall
exam: When the UV index is 3 or higher, what should you do? | *Wear sunscreen and a hat, and sit in the shade | Lie in the sun for longer to get a tan | Go out at midday with no protection | Only wear sunglasses when it is raining
